# Slurm's per-job stdout/stderr (run.sbatch and run_smoketest.sbatch point
# their -o/-e here). One pair of files per job ID, specific to one run on one
# cluster -- never worth sharing.
#
# This file is the one exception to its own rule, and exists so git keeps the
# directory itself: sbatch fails outright if the -o/-e directory does not
# already exist, so it has to survive a fresh clone.
*
!.gitignore
